READING OF THIS RUN
  CDC-1 is correct in both directions and scores C1.
  CDC-2 is WRONG in both directions, and the cause is the declaration, not the
  design. `inc` is a control input in the same domain; it is not the thing that
  crosses. The bus that crosses is the one feeding s1, which is `gray` in gold
  and `bin` in gate. Declaring `inc` made the gate measure the depth of the
  counter itself, which is 1 in gold (bin has no second stage) and 3 in gate
  (bin -> s1 -> s2 is a direct chain once the encoder moves away). Both numbers
  are real measurements of the wrong question.
  Prompted amendment 2. This run is kept.
